{"authored" [{"question" "q-347193" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The position vector $r(t)$ of a particle $P$ relative to a fixed origin $O$ at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨{t}^{3}-2t,\\,{t}^{4}-2{t}^{2}⟩.\n$$\n\nCalculate the components of the acceleration vector $a$ at time $t.$\n\n$a=⟨${{field-1}},{{field-2}}$⟩$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "f0a2c2880a06951eefab841dca7837295f0502d351b00024f3d1b7cfcb08fc59" "basis" 2031 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-347193" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the acceleration vector, we need to differentiate the velocity vector. So first, we need to compute the velocity vector, which we can do by differentiating the position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}-2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{4}-2{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3{t}^{2}-2,\\,4{t}^{3}-4t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2}-2),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{3}-4t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6t,\\,12{t}^{2}-4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "f0a2c2880a06951eefab841dca7837295f0502d351b00024f3d1b7cfcb08fc59" "basis" 2031 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-347193" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c439abc6883a4f52d0bd42ea0cda5d833848215aa1a4c9b36a353704806da4c3" "basis" 2031 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-347193" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "f0a2c2880a06951eefab841dca7837295f0502d351b00024f3d1b7cfcb08fc59" "basis" 2031 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-347193" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6t"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "f0a2c2880a06951eefab841dca7837295f0502d351b00024f3d1b7cfcb08fc59" "basis" 2031 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-347193" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "f0a2c2880a06951eefab841dca7837295f0502d351b00024f3d1b7cfcb08fc59" "basis" 2031 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-347193" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "12t^2-4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "f0a2c2880a06951eefab841dca7837295f0502d351b00024f3d1b7cfcb08fc59" "basis" 2031 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-85609" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The position vector $r$ of a particle $P$ relative to a fixed origin $O$ at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨{e}^{2-t},\\,3+{t}^{4}⟩.\n$$\n\nCalculate the acceleration vector $a$ at time $t=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063991/state.json" "file_sha256" "c69773e4a8395edb571b6d107a6f2d618656105cfe07b4ad682daa2d37ef971c"} {"question" "q-85609" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the acceleration vector, we need to differentiate the velocity vector. So first, we need to compute the velocity vector, which we can do this by differentiating the position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{2-t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3+{t}^{4})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-{e}^{2-t},\\,4{t}^{3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-{e}^{2-t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{2-t},\\,12{t}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the acceleration at time $t=2,$ we substitute $t=2$ into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(2) & =⟨{e}^{2-2},12(2)^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,48⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063991/state.json" "file_sha256" "c69773e4a8395edb571b6d107a6f2d618656105cfe07b4ad682daa2d37ef971c"} {"question" "q-85609" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063991/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ce5ee6f4e4aa02d21fd404508945c3a6c0d56543a2529c95d71d5898ae143c07"} {"question" "q-85609" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063991/state.json" "file_sha256" "c69773e4a8395edb571b6d107a6f2d618656105cfe07b4ad682daa2d37ef971c"} {"question" "q-85609" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "a(2)=⟨-1,24⟩"] ["math" "a(2)=⟨0,24⟩"] ["math" "a(2)=⟨0,48⟩"] ["math" "a(2)=⟨1,48⟩"] ["math" "a(2)=⟨1,96⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063991/state.json" "file_sha256" "c69773e4a8395edb571b6d107a6f2d618656105cfe07b4ad682daa2d37ef971c"} {"question" "q-85609" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "a(2)=⟨1,48⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063991/state.json" "file_sha256" "c69773e4a8395edb571b6d107a6f2d618656105cfe07b4ad682daa2d37ef971c"} {"question" "q-121908" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The velocity vector $v=⟨u,v⟩$ of a particle $P$ at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nv=⟨3t-1,\\sqrt{2t+1}⟩,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the acceleration vector $a$ at time $t=4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063991/state.json" "file_sha256" "c69773e4a8395edb571b6d107a6f2d618656105cfe07b4ad682daa2d37ef971c"} {"question" "q-121908" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t-1),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{2t+1})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2t+1}}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the acceleration at time $t=4,$ we substitute $t=4$ into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(4) & =⟨3,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2(4)+1}}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{9}}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\frac{1}{3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063991/state.json" "file_sha256" "c69773e4a8395edb571b6d107a6f2d618656105cfe07b4ad682daa2d37ef971c"} {"question" "q-121908" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063991/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ce5ee6f4e4aa02d21fd404508945c3a6c0d56543a2529c95d71d5898ae143c07"} {"question" "q-121908" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063991/state.json" "file_sha256" "c69773e4a8395edb571b6d107a6f2d618656105cfe07b4ad682daa2d37ef971c"} {"question" "q-121908" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "a(4)=⟨11,\\sqrt{3}⟩"] ["math" "a(4)=⟨3,\\frac{1}{3}⟩"] ["math" "a(4)=⟨3,\\sqrt{3}⟩"] ["math" "a(4)=⟨4,\\frac{1}{3}⟩"] ["math" "a(4)=⟨4,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063991/state.json" "file_sha256" "c69773e4a8395edb571b6d107a6f2d618656105cfe07b4ad682daa2d37ef971c"} {"question" "q-121908" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "a(4)=⟨3,\\frac{1}{3}⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063991/state.json" "file_sha256" "c69773e4a8395edb571b6d107a6f2d618656105cfe07b4ad682daa2d37ef971c"} {"question" "q-121931" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The position vector $r(t)$ of a particle $P$ relative to a fixed origin $O$ at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨4t-{t}^{3},2{t}^{2}+t⟩.\n$$\n\nCalculate the acceleration vector $a.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063991/state.json" "file_sha256" "c69773e4a8395edb571b6d107a6f2d618656105cfe07b4ad682daa2d37ef971c"} {"question" "q-121931" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the acceleration vector, we need to differentiate the velocity vector. So first, we need to compute the velocity vector, which we can do this by differentiating the position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t-{t}^{3}),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{2}+t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4-3{t}^{2},4t+1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4-3{t}^{2}),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t+1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-6t,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063991/state.json" "file_sha256" "c69773e4a8395edb571b6d107a6f2d618656105cfe07b4ad682daa2d37ef971c"} {"question" "q-121931" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063991/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ce5ee6f4e4aa02d21fd404508945c3a6c0d56543a2529c95d71d5898ae143c07"} {"question" "q-121931" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063991/state.json" "file_sha256" "c69773e4a8395edb571b6d107a6f2d618656105cfe07b4ad682daa2d37ef971c"} {"question" "q-121931" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "a=⟨-3{t}^{2},2⟩"] ["math" "a=⟨-3{t}^{2},4⟩"] ["math" "a=⟨-4t,4t+1⟩"] ["math" "a=⟨-6t,4t+1⟩"] ["math" "a=⟨-6t,4⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063991/state.json" "file_sha256" "c69773e4a8395edb571b6d107a6f2d618656105cfe07b4ad682daa2d37ef971c"} {"question" "q-121931" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "a=⟨-6t,4⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063991/state.json" "file_sha256" "c69773e4a8395edb571b6d107a6f2d618656105cfe07b4ad682daa2d37ef971c"} {"question" "q-347193" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The position vector $r(t)$ of a particle $P$ relative to a fixed origin $O$ at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨{t}^{3}-2t,\\,{t}^{4}-2{t}^{2}⟩.\n$$\n\nCalculate the components of the acceleration vector $a$ at time $t.$\n\n$a=⟨${{field-1}},{{field-2}}$⟩$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063991/state.json" "file_sha256" "c69773e4a8395edb571b6d107a6f2d618656105cfe07b4ad682daa2d37ef971c"} {"question" "q-347193" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the acceleration vector, we need to differentiate the velocity vector. So first, we need to compute the velocity vector, which we can do by differentiating the position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}-2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{4}-2{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3{t}^{2}-2,\\,4{t}^{3}-4t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2}-2),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{3}-4t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6t,\\,12{t}^{2}-4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063991/state.json" "file_sha256" "c69773e4a8395edb571b6d107a6f2d618656105cfe07b4ad682daa2d37ef971c"} {"question" "q-347193" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063991/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ce5ee6f4e4aa02d21fd404508945c3a6c0d56543a2529c95d71d5898ae143c07"} {"question" "q-347193" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063991/state.json" "file_sha256" "c69773e4a8395edb571b6d107a6f2d618656105cfe07b4ad682daa2d37ef971c"} {"question" "q-347193" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6t"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063991/state.json" "file_sha256" "c69773e4a8395edb571b6d107a6f2d618656105cfe07b4ad682daa2d37ef971c"} {"question" "q-347193" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063991/state.json" "file_sha256" "c69773e4a8395edb571b6d107a6f2d618656105cfe07b4ad682daa2d37ef971c"} {"question" "q-347193" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "12t^2-4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063991/state.json" "file_sha256" "c69773e4a8395edb571b6d107a6f2d618656105cfe07b4ad682daa2d37ef971c"} {"question" "q-347197" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The position vector $r$ of a particle $P$ relative to a fixed origin $O$ at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨{t}^{3}-2{t}^{2}+1,\\,4+{t}^{2}-{t}^{3}⟩.\n$$\n\nCalculate the components of the acceleration vector $a$ at time $t=0.$ Do not round the answers.\n\n$a(0)=⟨${{field-1}},{{field-2}}$⟩$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063991/state.json" "file_sha256" "c69773e4a8395edb571b6d107a6f2d618656105cfe07b4ad682daa2d37ef971c"} {"question" "q-347197" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the acceleration vector, we need to differentiate the velocity vector. So first, we need to compute the velocity vector, which we can do by differentiating the position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}-2{t}^{2}+1),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4+{t}^{2}-{t}^{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3{t}^{2}-4t,\\,2t-3{t}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2}-4t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t-3{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6t-4,\\,2-6t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the acceleration at time $t=0,$ we substitute $t=0$ into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(0) & =⟨6(0)-4,\\,2-6(0)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063991/state.json" "file_sha256" "c69773e4a8395edb571b6d107a6f2d618656105cfe07b4ad682daa2d37ef971c"} {"question" "q-347197" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063991/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ce5ee6f4e4aa02d21fd404508945c3a6c0d56543a2529c95d71d5898ae143c07"} {"question" "q-347197" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063991/state.json" "file_sha256" "c69773e4a8395edb571b6d107a6f2d618656105cfe07b4ad682daa2d37ef971c"} {"question" "q-347197" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063991/state.json" "file_sha256" "c69773e4a8395edb571b6d107a6f2d618656105cfe07b4ad682daa2d37ef971c"} {"question" "q-347197" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063991/stat